# The doors one major's documents list and another major's do not, one line per fact.
#
#   major ~ document ~ symbol ~ reason
#
# Read by .dev/validate/documentation.sh. This is not a suppression list: every line is a claim the run has
# to satisfy. A gap with no line here fails the check, and a line here that matched nothing fails it just as
# loudly — the document has caught up, so the line has to go. Without that second half the list accumulates
# dead entries and eventually excuses a real omission that happens to land on a symbol something else
# already documented.
#
# Wildcards are refused rather than supported. An entry written as a pattern grows silently to cover the
# next gap, which is the whole failure it exists to prevent.
#
# Fields are trimmed, so the columns may be aligned. The reason is mandatory: a line whose reason is empty
# is a line nobody can review.
#
# The list is empty since the stabilization sweep closed the last v3 row: every door a major's documents
# list is now listed by every major that ships it. A new line here is a new divergence, and it needs the
# same one-line-per-fact form and a reason.
